    description: "**Defect.** A documented dataflow field, `dest_access_mode`, is populated on a tiny fraction of edges and is always the same value.\n\n**Evidence.** `dest_access_mode` is declared (ir.py:659) as an ADR-0015 dataflow attribute validated against VALID_ACCESS_MODES. It is populated on 113/110533 edges (0.10%) — calls 10 plus event_publishes 103 — all value 'read', never write/mutate/delete.\n\n**Contract.** A dataflow access-mode field should be populated across dataflow edges with the real direction (read/write/mutate/delete), so taint/dataflow direction can be read off it.\n\n**Consequence.** Dataflow/taint-direction reasoning that depends on this field is unsupported on 99.9% of edges and uninformative where present.\n\n**Related (not duplicate).** Sibling of INV-virik (reserved provenance fields never populated) and INV-lifik (constant-value fields), but dest_access_mode is a distinct dataflow field named in neither."  # 4472
    fields: {}  # 4472
